# Target C-II stale global-face endpoint regression (2026-09-12)

**Classification:** rejected stale endpoint target / regression.  This is a
proof-only correction; it does not change theorem-state authority.  The
repository state is `audit.46`, and C-II remains open.

## Exact conflict

An older provenance report,
`docs/reports/target_c_zs_strict_terminal_cut_domination_2026-09-09.md`, identifies
the strict global face inequality

\[
 b+Q>2h
\]

with the train surplus target `T-h>2f`.  That target cannot be the strict
endpoint of the current train/face ledger when `f` is the canonical bounded
nonquadrilateral-face count.

The active train-closure package records the exact finite identities

\[
 T=\frac{b+Q}{2}+2f,
 \qquad
 \frac{b+Q}{2}=h-s_Z,
\]

where `s_Z\ge 0` is the mixed-rigidity surplus.  Therefore

\[
 T=h-s_Z+2f,
 \qquad
 T-h-2f=-s_Z\le 0.
\]

Consequently the strict claim `T-h>2f` is algebraically impossible under the
same canonical definitions.  In the equality case `s_Z=0`, the ledger gives
`T-h=2f`, not a strict inequality.  This is an exact normalization/endpoint
regression, not a numerical issue.

The scope is the old report's identification of its `f` with the canonical
bounded nonquadrilateral-face count.  A differently defined exceptional-face
quantity would require a separate translation theorem; this note does not
rule out such a theorem.

## Consequence for the live C-II route

The old report is retained as provenance, but its strict endpoint must not be
used as a premise or as the next obligation.  The current canonical target is
the aggregate detour/source inequality coupling

\[
 \sum_r(L_r-2d_r)
\]

to `e_{BB}-k`, together with the separate protected-spare-capacity branch for
macroscopically inactive Type-I chambers.  The regression does not disprove
Level I, does not produce a C-II counterexample, and does not close C-II.

No `docs/STATE.md`, theorem-state, route-map, prompt, or generated-artifact
file is changed here because this correction does not promote a theorem or
change the canonical frontier.

